cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these lessons or their code, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Transformers from scratch to production and Transformer architectures from BERT to diffusion"
abstract: >-
  Two courses as notebooks that run on the free GPUs of Kaggle and Colab. The first builds an English-to-Russian
  translator with a Transformer written from scratch, then evaluates, tunes, packages and serves it and ships it as a
  reproducible Docker image. The second rebuilds the architectures that followed, from BERT, GPT and T5 to modern
  LLMs, mixture of experts, the KV cache and latent attention, long context, state space models and the Vision
  Transformer, with the code checked against reference implementations and published weights.
authors:
